title: Tackle Tool Call API Surface Tasks
status: draft
created: 2026-10-29
author: adrian
items[12]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,Naming types and strict scheme,"Add `invokables/tool_name.rs` with `InvokableName`, `WireToolName`, `NamespaceSeparator`, `ToolNameScheme`, and `StrictToolNameScheme`. Implement dot-to-`__` namespace encoding, invalid-character replacement with `_`, the configured maximum length, the 8-hex SHA-256 suffix, decode, and precise errors for empty or impossible names.","Unit tests cover the readable default, literal single and double underscores, non-ASCII input, empty names, and limits too small for a prefix plus hash. The same input and scheme always produce the same wire name.",high,4-6h,,"canonical-and-wire-separation,tool-name-scheme,readable-encoding,determinism,readable-default,ambiguous-underscores,empty-name,limit-too-small,non-ascii-name,no-silent-drops"
  T-002,Remaining schemes and custom pattern,"Add `GeminiToolNameScheme`, `MetaToolNameScheme`, `CohereToolNameScheme`, and `CustomToolNameScheme`. Encode and decode per scheme, including Gemini leading-character and dot rules, Meta single-dot handling, Cohere leading-digit rejection, and a custom pattern with optional maximum length.","Each scheme has round-trip and rejection tests. Custom patterns reject empty or malformed expressions. Selecting an unimplemented surface scheme is rejected by the scheme factory.",medium,3-5h,"T-001","tool-name-scheme,custom-scheme-and-pattern,surface-defaults,invalid-custom-pattern,unimplemented-surface-scheme"
  T-003,Per-request ToolNameMap,"Implement `ToolNameMap` with forward and reverse maps. Support forward entries for current model-invokable names and for history tool call and result names. `encode` allocates a unique wire name and appends a hash suffix on collision or truncation. `decode` consults only the current model-invokable set and returns `None` for unknown wire names.","Collisions and truncation produce distinct stable names; history names encode; unknown decode returns `None`; the map is request-local; dispatch cannot resolve a name outside the current set.",high,3-5h,"T-001,T-002","tool-name-map,canonical-and-wire-separation,request-local-state,collision-handling,length-and-truncation,historical-tool-not-current,unknown-call-passthrough,dispatch-safety"
  T-004,Registry render entry point,"Add `RenderedTools { tools, manifest, names }` and `Registry::render_tools(scheme)`. Render model-invokable tools and the system-prompt manifest with wire names. Keep direct invocation, ACP command advertisement, and dispatch on canonical names.","Every manifest name appears in the tool definitions and vice versa. Direct invocation and command advertisement still use canonical names. Registry tests pass with the rendered entry point.",medium,2-4h,"T-003","registry-render-entry-point,wire-named-manifest,manifest-matches-tools,canonical-and-wire-separation"
  T-005,Endpoint and model configuration schema,"Add `ToolNamesConfig`, `ModelConfig`, and `ToolNameSchemeName`. Replace `EndpointConfig.models` with a normalized map that accepts both `models = [...]` and `models.<name>` tables. Add endpoint-level `tool_names` and per-model `models.<name>.tool_names`.","Both model forms parse to the same map. Existing list-form configurations still load. Unknown fields and invalid scheme names fail with the endpoint and model named. `pattern` without `custom` fails validation.",high,3-5h,"T-002","endpoint-and-model-configuration,backward-compatibility,list-compatibility,quoted-model-keys,scheme-and-pattern-conflict"
  T-006,Scheme resolution and precedence,"Add `config/tool_names.rs` with `resolve_tool_names(endpoint, model)`. Resolve model override over endpoint override over wire-format default. Validate `custom` plus `pattern`, reject unimplemented surface schemes, and return a precise error naming the endpoint and model.","Unit tests cover every precedence branch, strict defaults for OpenAI chat and Anthropic messages, the Gemini default for the future Google surface, and each validation failure.",medium,2-4h,"T-005","endpoint-and-model-configuration,surface-defaults,custom-scheme-and-pattern,configuration-precedence,invalid-custom-pattern,scheme-and-pattern-conflict,unimplemented-surface-scheme"
  T-007,Turn preparation and provider construction,"Resolve the scheme in `prepare_turn` after `model_ref` is known. Call `Registry::render_tools`, pass the `ToolNameMap` into `provider_for`, and carry wire-named tools and system prompt in `LoopInputs`. Update the `/context` builders in ACP v1 and v2 to use the same rendered tools and manifest.","A turn uses the selected scheme; `/context` reports the same wire names as the model request; direct invocation paths remain canonical; no caller builds tools without a scheme.",medium,3-5h,"T-004,T-006","registry-render-entry-point,wire-named-manifest,provider-encode-and-decode,surface-defaults,configuration-precedence"
  T-008,Provider history encoding and response decoding,"Store the `ToolNameMap` on `RigProvider`. Change `rig::to_rig_message` to encode historical tool call and result names and `rig::tool_calls_of` to decode model tool calls. Leave unknown wire names unchanged so the existing unknown-invokable path handles them.","A strict-scheme turn sends safe wire names, decodes the model call to canonical, and executes the canonical tool. `ModelResponse.tool_calls` never contains a wire name. Unknown wire names and canonical-name hallucinations pass through. Provider unit tests cover history and response paths.",high,4-6h,"T-003,T-007","provider-encode-and-decode,canonical-persistence,strict-provider-tool-call,unknown-call-passthrough,model-returns-canonical-name,dispatch-safety"
  T-009,Static model list and config call sites,"Update `agent/config_options.rs` to use normalized map keys for the static model fallback. Update `cli/auth.rs`, `agent/script_loop.rs`, provider tests, and any `EndpointConfig` construction from `models: Vec::new()` to the default map. Preserve discovery failure notices.","Model discovery failure still falls back to the configured static list. Notices are unchanged. All constructors compile and existing config tests pass with the list form.",low,1-2h,"T-005","endpoint-and-model-configuration,backward-compatibility,list-compatibility"
  T-010,Lossy rewrite warnings,"Emit `tracing::warn!()` only for truncation and hash suffixes. Include the canonical name, wire name, endpoint, model, and surface. Deduplicate per endpoint, model, and canonical name. Routine dot and invalid-character rewrites stay silent.","Tests capture exactly one warning for a lossy name across repeated requests, no warning for a routine namespace rewrite, and the expected fields on the warning.",low,1-3h,"T-003,T-006","lossy-rewrite-warnings,observability,lossy-warning-only"
  T-011,End-to-end and integration coverage,"Add a turn-level test with a dotted MCP tool through a strict endpoint. Verify the model is offered a safe name, the tool executes, storage and telemetry contain only canonical names, the manifest matches the tools, unknown calls pass through, and an impossible name fails without dropping the tool.","The integration test passes against a recorded strict endpoint. No wire name appears in the session DAG. The unknown-call and impossible-name paths return the specified errors.",high,4-6h,"T-008,T-009,T-010","strict-provider-tool-call,canonical-persistence,manifest-matches-tools,unknown-call-passthrough,impossible-name-fails,testability,performance,dispatch-safety"
  T-012,Documentation,"Update `docs/docs/user/tackle/reference/config.mdx` with endpoint and per-model `tool_names`, list and table model forms, precedence, and the custom pattern escape hatch. Update `docs/docs/user/tackle/tools.mdx` with wire naming, warnings, and strict-provider behavior.","The docs include working TOML examples for list-form models, table-form models, endpoint defaults, per-model overrides, and custom patterns. The tools page explains canonical versus wire names and the warning behavior.",low,1-2h,"T-006,T-008","endpoint-and-model-configuration,surface-defaults,custom-scheme-and-pattern,lossy-rewrite-warnings,backward-compatibility"
